<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  page="support"
  title="Support — InFocus"
  description="Help with InFocus: alarms, sounds with the phone locked, Live Activities, Siri, language and exporting your history."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p class="lede">Questions, bugs or ideas? Email <a href="mailto:support@infocustempo.com">support@infocustempo.com</a>. I answer in English or Spanish, usually within two business days.</p>
  <p>It helps to include your iPhone model, iOS version and what you were timing.</p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>The alarm didn't ring at the end of a focus block</summary>
    <p>Open the iPhone Settings app → Apps → InFocus and make sure Alarms are allowed. If you declined alarms, InFocus uses notifications instead, which may stay quiet in Silent mode or during a Focus. Allow them in the same place.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>I can't hear the beeps when the phone is locked</summary>
    <p>Check that Sounds or Voice is on in InFocus → Settings, and that your iPhone volume is up. With both turned off, InFocus doesn't play audio in the background; the alarm at the end of the workout still rings.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>The timer doesn't show on the Lock Screen</summary>
    <p>Open the iPhone Settings app → Apps → InFocus and turn on Live Activities.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I start a timer with Siri?</summary>
    <p>Say “Hey Siri, start a Pomodoro in InFocus” or “Start a Tabata in InFocus”. You can also start any saved preset by name, or add these actions in the Shortcuts app and to the Action button.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I change the app's language?</summary>
    <p>InFocus follows your iPhone's language. To use a different one just for InFocus, open the Settings app → Apps → InFocus → Language.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I keep a copy of my history?</summary>
    <p>Yes. In InFocus, tap the gear, then Export history, to save or send a CSV file you can open in Numbers or Excel.</p>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How do I delete my data?</summary>
    <p>Everything lives on your iPhone. You can delete single sessions in History, or delete the app to remove all of it. Nothing is stored anywhere else.</p>
  </details>
</BaseLayout>
